# Screen layouts

There are four layouts. 行動端 is tablet and phone together. 手機端 is the phone only.

| Layout | When it applies |
| --- | --- |
| 網頁端直向 | Outer width ≥ 900px, portrait. The app sits in the 1× iframe. |
| 網頁端橫向 | Outer width ≥ 900px, landscape. Same iframe. |
| 平板端 | 行動端 (`max-width: 899px`) and not 手機端. Android tablets around 600px wide, and landscape tablets scaled to about 640×400, stay here. |
| 手機端 | Not tablet hardware, and (`max-width: 480px`, or landscape and `max-height: 410px` and `max-width: 899px`). No aspect-ratio test. |

- 行動端 CSS is `@media (max-width: 899px)`. Do not raise 899. Do not use 1100. A 1400px desktop window at 1× is 1400px wide and stays 網頁端.
- iPad landscape (outer 1024) becomes an iframe about 682×512 (mobile 1.5× frame). That is 平板端. iPad Pro 12.9 landscape (outer 1366) becomes about 911px wide and stays 網頁端.
- Phone rules come after the 899 block. Portrait phones are at most 480px wide. Landscape phones are short (`max-height: 410px`) without an aspect-ratio test. Tablet hardware is decided by screen area (`>= 500000` CSS px²), not aspect ratio; those devices get `html.is-ua-tablet` and stay 平板端.
- Tablet portrait fill uses `min-width: 481px` inside the 899 block. Do not treat 481–899px as a phone.
- 平板端橫向 keeps the 網頁端橫向 layout. The `max-width: 899px` and `max-width: 900px` layout rules apply only in portrait, or on 手機端. Card dragging on 平板端橫向 still uses the touch long-press in `src/lib/touchDrag.ts` (`max-width: 899px`). Do not switch those cards back to mouse-only dragging.
- 手機端 landscape: `PhonePortraitLock` fills the viewport with「請將手機直向使用，以獲得較佳的體驗。」and locks the page underneath until portrait. Rotating a phone must not `location.reload()` (keeps in-memory work). Phone stand preview uses a taller viewport (100px) and lowers the tent so the title does not cover the card. Phone master assign/setup pages lock outer overflow (`100dvh`); seating choose fixed at 40vh (preview takes the rest) with sticky actions; seating mode tile fonts scaled down; all print previews hide「開始列印」and style 下載為PDF green/right; attendance palette fixed at 45vh and 多選／範圍 sit in the seat grid after #30; room assign folders use a 3-column landscape (3×2) board with 3:2 slots.
- 平板端: Portrait desk/badge confirm and mode/booth choose at zoom 1. Landscape: homepage 0.7; confirm / master map 0.7; import header 0.7; mode-choose and master assign headers 0.7; desk/badge editor toolbar + subbar + corner actions 0.7; editor stage supports empty-drag pan + pinch zoom; item mini-bar fixed at un-pinched ×3 for desk / ×1 for badge / ×1.5 for expo badge (does not grow with editor pinch zoom); mode/booth choose body 0.65; seating setup hides step/preview labels and zooms `.booth-main` to 0.65; layout grid count inputs ×1.5; seating assign corner actions ×1.5; pages print bar 0.9, seat print bar 0.7; seat print stage 0.65. Portrait desk booth keeps preview on top and choose below. Landscape booth (desk reference, do not change) and seating setup: preview left, choose right; stand preview top-left at phone width with tall enough viewport. Confirm-page preview uses the phone range slider on tablet landscape. Landscape assign keeps map|pool side-by-side (do not stack via max-width 860). Seating assign: pool `40vw`, map and pool `zoom: 0.65`; classroom preview keeps aspect ratio and fills the map container (`min(100cqi, 100cqb × paper ratio)`). Bus assign pool `40vw` with ~56px cards; pool head/list and `.bus-info` zoom 0.65; scroll right padding tightened so bus chart can scale to fill height (info overlays top-right); chart left-aligned in stage. Sweep assign toolbar, duty zone, and pool zoom 0.65. Attendance edit: stage (快拉+封裝) and palette (卡片區) zoom 0.65. Room setup list is 2×3 (five drafts leave the last cell empty on the left); only the top-left draft stays enabled by default. Room assign pool and Sweep assign (duty board + pool/task panels) use a custom scrollbar rail: 5px visual, 10px hit area (always visible; thumb/wheel scroll gain ×2). On tablet landscape, choose pages (desk booth/mode pick, seating setup, room setup) use the same rail when content overflows (`hideRailWhenFit`). On tablet landscape, rooms over 6 beds use 2-column wrap inside each folder (`.is-wide` forced to 2 cols).
- Shared import/confirm chrome: desk plate (`is-desk`) is the reference. Other Excel→ConfirmFields tools use `is-flow` so the same phone/tablet upload+map rules apply (`:is(.app.is-desk…, .app.is-flow…)`). RoomTool only gets `is-flow` on upload (its `step-map` is RoomSetup, not ConfirmFields). Choose/booth/edit/stand stay desk-only.
- Tablet portrait confirm preview rows stay content-height (no flex-stretched preview chips). The preview tbody is `flex: 0 1 auto`, so the horizontal range (tfoot) sits right under the last preview row, not at the bottom of the preview box. Seating setup on tablet portrait locks preview at 50dvh with choose taking the rest, and the page is `100dvh` with `min-height: 0`. The choose scroller is at least as tall as that panel, so the buttons sit at its lower left when the step fits. When the step is taller, only that panel scrolls, far enough to clear the bottom safe area. Desk booth on portrait is `height: 100dvh` with `min-height: 0`, so `min-height: 100vh` cannot push the buttons below the visible page when the browser bar is showing. The choose scroller is at least as tall as the panel, so the buttons sit at its lower left when the step fits. When the step is taller, that same panel scrolls far enough to clear the bottom safe area.
- 大師 tools (Seating, Bus, Sweep, Room) put `is-master` on the app root at every step. In tablet portrait, html/body with `.app.is-master` get `overflow: hidden` to lock the outer scrollbar without changing the layout. Bus and Seating assign card areas (`.seat-pool`) are fixed at 30vh on tablet portrait; cards stay 72px and fill more rows. Attendance cards use the same touch long-press drag as other mobile cards (`.att-card` in `touchDrag.ts`).
- Browser kind lives in `detectBrowser()` (`src/lib/screenLayout.ts`). Order: Edge, Samsung, Opera, Firefox, Chrome (incl. CriOS), Safari, else 其他. Prefer `navigator.userAgentData.brands` when present, then fall back to `userAgent`.
- Mobile UA lives in `detectMobile()`. Trust `userAgentData.mobile === true` only; do not treat `false` as Desktop (Android tablets often report false). Also match Android (phone or tablet), iPhone/iPod/iPad/Tablet/Silk, iPadOS MacIntel+touch, or coarse pointer + hover:none + multi-touch (desktop-site spoofing). PC Chrome with a mouse stays Desktop.
- Phone vs tablet: `detectDeviceKind()` uses `detectTablet()` when mobile and max-width 899 (UA iPad/Tablet/Silk, or total CSS px² via `deviceAreaPx()` ≥ 500000). Inside the scaled iframe (`?ui=1`), area uses the outer window (e.g. mobile 1.5× inner 775×421 → outer ~1163×632≈735k → 平板端). Unframed phone 390×875≈341k → 手機端. Explicit iPad UA stays 平板端 even if the viewport area is under 500000, so landscape is not locked by PhonePortraitLock. No aspect-ratio tests.
- Desktop UA (`!detectMobile()`) is always 網頁端: `detectDeviceKind()` returns 網頁端 first, and `main.tsx` always mounts the 1× iframe (never the compact direct app). If outer width would be under 900px, the desktop iframe keeps a 900px-wide inner viewport and lowers zoom so PC Chrome cannot fall into 平板端. Mobile UA still uses the existing 899 / phone viewport rules (wide mobile still uses the 1.5× frame).
